          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        },
        {
          "id": "motivates",
          "key": "motivates",
          "label": "motivates",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 0,
          "role": "relationship",
          "allowedEdgeTypes": [
            "reference"
          ],
          "metadata": {
            "relationship": true,
            "role": "relationship"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "affects",
          "key": "affects",
          "label": "affects",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 180,
          "role": "relationship",
          "allowedEdgeTypes": [
            "reference"
          ],
          "metadata": {
            "relationship": true,
            "role": "relationship"
          },
          "portId": "affects"
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "A Method Is a Script With a Nametag",
        "statement": "A Method node today is a name, some source, a parameters list of labels, and an allowMutations flag. The runner gives its source a frozen api.invocation object and takes the return value as the result. Nothing states what the Method needs, what it may change, or what happened when it ran. The flag that looks like a safety setting is not one: outside dry runs the host applies calls such as updateNode and createNode whether or not allowMutations is set. Only dry runs consult it, and only sendHandoff refuses without it.",
        "impact": "The Handler editor can only say \"Read-only execution\" or \"May update graph state\" from that flag, which promises more than the runtime enforces. A reviewer cannot tell what a Method touches, one Method cannot be reused safely from Handlers with differently shaped events, and a dry run has nothing to be checked against.",
        "urgency": "high",
        "definitionKey": "idea-problem",
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "idea-problem",
          "sourceRef": "github://mikemartinez1974/public/templates/idea-template/classes/nodes/idea-problem.node-class.node",
