      "data": {
        "title": "Give the Method a contract and each call an identity",
        "description": "Inputs: a short list of named inputs read from the occurrence payload by name; a missing required input fails the Invocation before any code runs and names the input. Effects: a short list of coarse kinds the Method may perform (update node, create node, delete node, edges, emit event, hand off), each with optional target nodes; the host refuses calls outside the list, and allowMutations becomes derived from it. Invocation: every call is an explicit runtime entity with an id, the Method, the caller (Handler and position), the arguments, the mode (dry or live), and its cause (occurrence, root occurrence and delivery), exposed to the source as the frozen api.invocation. It is not persisted as a node. Outcome: each Invocation reports status, result or error, duration and attempted effects, keyed by the invocation id; a dry run returns the proposed effects instead of applying them. Authority: a call runs only where what the Method declares, what the caller may do, and what the runtime permits all agree. The Method card shows its last outcome, and the Handler shows a read-only summary of its Methods' declared effects.",
        "differentiator": "Small enough to write by hand, enforced at the one place every mutation already passes through, so a declaration is a limit and not only a description. Identity now and lifecycle later: the effects of one Invocation can be followed to the Event they emit, which answers why something happened.",
        "definitionKey": "idea-proposed-approach",
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "idea-proposed-approach",
          "sourceRef": "github://mikemartinez1974/public/templates/idea-template/classes/nodes/idea-proposed-approach.node-class.node",
