          ],
          "metadata": {
            "relationship": true,
            "role": "relationship"
          }
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "Persist Invocation nodes and a full lifecycle now",
        "description": "Store each call as a graph node with a lifecycle (requested, authorized, running, succeeded, failed, cancelled), progress, cancellation and history, as sketched in the discussion on the Methods topic.",
        "tradeoffs": "The right shape for long-running Personal Server Methods and for tracing across graphs, but it is a storage and runtime design of its own. Handler-invoked Methods that finish do not need it yet. What they do need is the identity, which is why it is kept: Invocation is explicit now, and persistence and lifecycle are what is deferred.",
        "definitionKey": "idea-alternative",
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "idea-alternative",
