      "data": {
        "view": {
          "intent": "node",
          "payload": "node.web.detail"
        },
        "semanticLevel": "detail",
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# A Solid Method Node\n\nA Method should be a small, reviewable contract: what it reads, what it may change, and what it reports. Each call is an explicit, ephemeral Invocation with an identity, so its Outcome and effects can be traced to the Event that caused it. What happens after a failure is the Handler's policy.\n\nThis builds on the Event Handler behavior idea, `github://mikemartinez1974/public/ideas/event-handler-behavior/root.node`."
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "ownsContent": true,
          "surfaceDelegation": true
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "method-node-design"
        }
      }
    },
